padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/PaulLee_AberrantComic1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/PaulLee_AberrantComic2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would buy only the complied <b>Aberrant</b> comic, just to understand whole relation of this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a 4 page comic opening the Secrets Chapter. The art is amazing and it shows how much of the Metaplot Mal knew, something I would not expect originally, but makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T13:58:10-07:00","id":1451901,"title":"","content":"From <b>Onyx Path Con</b> <b><i>Trinity Continuum</i></b> panel...<br /> <br /> In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451830-tc-aether\"><b>TC Aether</b> - 1890 steampunk era</a> - we will see Aeon Society of Max Mercer's parents - and themselves! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T16:09:31-07:00","id":1453317,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really looking forward to exploring the relationship between Max and Michael if I ever run Adventure!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m neither gay nor male irl, but I definitely think it\u2019s a fascinating and complicated love story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-23-2021, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T05:14:36-07:00","id":1453347,"title":"","content":"I think it would be cool if Max had his son from a tryst with a female friend (it can happen even if you\u2019re mostly ace), but even though he\u2019s probably really fond of her, he doesn\u2019t love her the way he loved Michael.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T06:28:03-07:00","id":1453356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1453347#post1453347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be cool if Max had his son from a tryst with a female friend (it can happen even if you\u2019re mostly ace), but even though he\u2019s probably really fond of her, he doesn\u2019t love her the way he loved Michael.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my general read the timeline as it is. Max is ace that loves Micheal - and just had 'accident' with one female friend, when they drunk a lot on party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-25-2021, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T13:54:41-07:00","id":1453404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1453356#post1453356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's my general read the timeline as it is. Max is ace that loves MIcheal - and just had 'accident' with one female friend, when they drunk a lot on party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. That makes a lot of sense. I was tryna decide if it should be like a fling or just an ONS, but I like your interpretation better. Makes Max and Michael\u2019s love for each other more solid and not one-sided if Max doesn\u2019t also have a relationship with a girl (even if it is just a brief fling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T05:52:05-08:00","id":1468748,"title":"","content":"In our game we decided that Michael Mercer who shows up and says he's Max's son is actually the Anti-Max trying to influence the Aeon Society for his own ends. Max at that point (if I'm remembering correctly) has withdrawn from public life so &quot;Michael&quot; steps in to adjust the course of the timeline. If you take that as the premise all of Max's descendants that show up in the later books are actually descended from Anti-Max even if they themselves think they are descended from Max. As we are currently playing in the Aeon/Psion age it has no direct influence on our game but until they release more information about Anti-Max it makes for some interesting lore brainstorming discussions in our group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T06:36:48-08:00","id":1468753,"title":"","content":"Well, there are 2 big options on his family tree<br /> <br /> 1. Margaret Mercer is Max granddaughter and Michael is his son (biological or not, probably biological because he is described as very similar)<br /> <br /> 2. Margaret is his daughter and Michael is Max himself. He pretends to be his own son, pretend to die and keep his old self identity but keeps his actual daughter in the shadow pretending to be his grandfather (that would not make much sense to me).<br /> <br /> In the 30s and later, I believe there was a significant number of people that pretended to be straight to fit in the society and avoid persecution (not all LGBT+ did it, but maybe he did). It was a matter of survival, he loved Michael, he probably did love him a lot, even named his son as Michael (even if he is Michael himself), but he probably got married and his wife eventually died of old age (he is immortal, the others not).<br /> <br /> Anti-Max is possibly himself, after many many years, trying to correct his own mistakes, with a point of view different as he has seen much more things than his younger self. This would be a plot similar to the one of Nozdromu becoming Murozond and starting the infinite dragon flight in WoW, after centuries of corruption (or in Max case centuries changing the timeline with qusestionable results)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T07:35:03-08:00","id":1468757,"title":"","content":"We discussed both of those actually. The implication in 1e was that Michael was Max himself from a earlier point in time. However for our game we decided that we like the story possibility's of Aeon better if there was a shadow war between Max and Anti-Max going on in the background of the setting with each running butterfly effect missions using Aeon personnel to change the future at cross purposes. It has nothing to do with Max being gay or ace or whatever, more of tailoring it to our group as we tend to run more spy or covert ops style games with intrigue and clouded motivations for even the best of intentioned missions.<br /> <br /> Spoilers ahead for Adventure! setting secrets.<br /> <br /> I may be mistaken as I don't have the book to check (I mainly haunt the forums while I have down time at work) but if I remember correctly doesn't it say in the setting secrets that Anti-Max is a creature that was feeding off the Flux energy released by Max on his first trip thru time that was influenced by all of the negative things it saw following him. At some point it had watched so much of Max that it decided to copy him becoming Anti-Max.Or something like that, I'm sure I'm getting some of the details wrong. I know in 1e Evil Max was a version of Max himself from an alternate timeline connected to 1e Aberrant in some way, but they dropped most if not all of that for 2e.<br /> <br /> The rational we had for Anti-Max being Michael was he wanted to experience what being human actually was like and not be defined by being just a copy of something else, hence the leaving of descendants. He is trying to steer the future to something that matches his outlook on life which is a bitter and cynical version of the bright and shinning future Max wants to lead the world to.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it comes down to what works for your group. We've had to change our &quot;cannon&quot; for our game every time a book comes out already, the way we play until it comes up in game nothing is set in stone and can change at the drop of the hat if it makes for a better story. Of course once someone encounters it in game it's set and the rest of the &quot;cannon&quot; has to take it into account when it changes.While it dose mean that we write ourselves into a corner every so often when newly released information contradicts something that has been established in-game as true so the other game master and I have to scramble for a reason both can be true at once (once we had to default to &quot;you were being lied to the entire time&quot; which changed the course of the entire campaign at that point) its fun and adds a layer of flexibility which comes in handy when the other game master and I trade off who's running the game.<br /> Hell that just happened with the latest release from the current Anima kick-starter. We had discussed how we were going to fit Anima into our overall metaplot and were comfortable with it until the chapter on allegiances dropped the other day and the info in that is making us reevaluate quite a few assumptions we had made about Aeon and refactor a large chunk of the campaign metaplot..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T15:27:58-07:00","id":1477548,"title":"","content":"It's funny 'Mercer Effect' is now real thing - in totally contrast to Trinity meaning of this phrase. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> In Trinity, it would be name for time jumping?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/screenrant.com/critical-role-dnd-mercer-effect-dungeons-dragons-expectations/amp/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/screenrant.com/critical-role-dnd-mercer-effect-dungeons-dragons-expectations/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/screenrant.com/critical-role-dnd-mercer-effect-dungeons-dragons-expectations/amp/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/amp/s/screenrant.com/critical-role-dnd-mercer-effect-dungeons-dragons-expectations/amp/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T17:49:03-07:00","id":1477551,"title":"","content":"Why does every one act like it is wierd to have a crush on someone of an incompatible orientation. Or that Max can love Divis Mal/Dr Primoris/Michael, just not in a romantic way but of a powerful friendship. I my self have fallen for people who were I.compatible orientation, infact my long time celebrity crush came out as lesbian then transitioned to male and has a six pack now... Talk about two things that could never be, still interested in his career as he is a fantastic actor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T18:40:17-07:00","id":1477555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477551#post1477551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does every one act like it is wierd to have a crush on someone of an incompatible orientation. Or that Max can love Divis Mal/Dr Primoris/Michael, just not in a romantic way but of a powerful friendship. I my self have fallen for people who were I.compatible orientation, infact my long time celebrity crush came out as lesbian then transitioned to male and has a six pack now... Talk about two things that could never be, still interested in his career as he is a fantastic actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what the designers are saying is that it\u2019s more empowering for Max to return Michael\u2019s feelings but to be unable to reciprocate them sexually because Max is ace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-27T19:04:42-07:00","id":1477557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477555#post1477555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what the designers are saying is that it\u2019s more empowering for Max to return Michael\u2019s feelings but to be unable to reciprocate them sexually because Max is ace.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fuck is an Ace, if you mean Asexual that's not much better than Max being heterosexual. Then it makes the whole Max's daughter thing some what insensere. Honestly I'm sick of every love having to be romantic love. Just because I love some one doesn't mean I want to fuck them. Some non romantic loves are more powerful than the romantic ones. But the whole Max/Michael thing I feel was supposed to be the great romantic tragedy of the series as a whole. <br /> This non romantic love between individuals that does turn into misunderstandings is not just a cliche, but a frequent event in real life as well. Hence why it often pops up, often fueled by the authors own experiences with these events. <br /> <br /> Hell my preference for &quot;tom boys&quot;, and desire for friendship first used to constantly end with me finding out the woman I was interested in were gay. Thank god I foundsome one and can stop worrying about dating and put an end to that nonsense.<br /> <br /> I mean my dream girl was Elliot Page before he transitioned, so I get the whole incompatible thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T00:45:33-07:00","id":1477571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477557#post1477557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fuck is an Ace, if you mean Asexual that's not much better than Max being heterosexual. Then it makes the whole Max's daughter thing some what insensere. Honestly I'm sick of every love having to be romantic love. Just because I love some one doesn't mean I want to fuck them. Some non romantic loves are more powerful than the romantic ones. But the whole Max/Michael thing I feel was supposed to be the great romantic tragedy of the series as a whole.<br /> <br /> This non romantic love between individuals that does turn into misunderstandings is not just a cliche, but a frequent event in real life as well. Hence why it often pops up, often fueled by the authors own experiences with these events. <br /> <br /> Hell my preference for &quot;tom boys&quot;, and desire for friendship first used to constantly end with me finding out the woman I was interested in were gay. Thank god I foundsome one and can stop worrying about dating and put an end to that nonsense.<br /> <br /> I mean my dream girl was Elliot Page before he transitioned, so I get the whole incompatible thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max had a daughter? I know he was supposed to have a son (Michael Mercer) but idk about a daughter. That being said, you can have a kid and still be asexual. And you can definitely have paternal/maternal feelings for someone.<br /> <br /> I get it. I liked a guy friend of mine who turned out to be gay. But I still think it\u2019s more empowering if Max returns Michael\u2019s feelings but can\u2019t consummate their relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 03-28-2022, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T14:03:32-07:00","id":1477595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477571#post1477571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Max had a daughter? I know he was supposed to have a son (Michael Mercer) but idk about a daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're talking about Michael Mercer's daughter, Margaret A. Mercer, who got a write-up on page 107 of Aberrant. As for Michael being Max's son, all we really know is that Max got disillusioned with his inability to influence history and withdrew from society, with his 'son' showing up at his home and taking over. He is described as being &quot;far more severe and goal oriented&quot; than his 'father'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T14:09:47-07:00","id":1477596,"title":"","content":"Unofficially, I interpret that as \u2018Max from another dimension turned up and took original Max\u2019s place for a while.\u2019","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T18:28:28-07:00","id":1477601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477596#post1477596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unofficially, I interpret that as \u2018Max from another dimension turned up and took original Max\u2019s place for a while.\u2019</div> </div> </div> </div>Then maybe Max from another dimension wasn\u2019t ace like original Max was (or was implied to be), which is how and why he got married and had a daughter (Margaret). Assuming your unofficial interpretation is accurate, of course. But I like it overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T19:14:21-07:00","id":1477603,"title":"","content":"I am politely reminding you you don\u2019t need to love to get married, you don\u2019t need to me married to have kids, and you don\u2019t need to accept your sexuality to be ok with other aspects of your life.<br /> <br /> In the time Max was born and the time we are discussing here there were lots of people living lives of lie to be accept by society, not only women were sexually repressed, men were forced to go to brothels with their fathers at young ages, and to those boys that didn\u2019t like women or didn\u2019t like the idea of prostitution, they were being raped by the prostitutes their fathers and friends were paying.<br /> <br /> Max can have kids and have lived for years married (between the 40s and the 80s) until his wife died of age or any disease in the gap between Adventure! and Aberrant, and yet being ace, gay, or any other sexual orientation, because by the time it was seen as wrong and sinful.<br /> <br /> I personally know more than one men in their 50s that after years married and having kids find out themselves as gay, just to leave their wives to embrace their sexuality and start dating man. And those are people that were born in the 60s and grew up after all the sexual revolution of the 60s and 70s. Imagine how many people denied their own self for their entire lives.<br /> <br /> In other words, summarizing, Max can be Ace and have kids, Max could be gay (actually love Michael romantically and sexually), not accept it (repressing his own sexuality) and have kids. Just don\u2019t say Max being *** would make it impossible for him to have biological kids (not to mention adoption).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T19:20:30-07:00","id":1477605,"title":"","content":"If we wanted an ACE why not the other pillar, the Proxy for the QK order. She is not listed as having any romantic interests, when she does pop up she is happily engaged in her work. Infact her last moments in the Adventure period was when Divas Mal spirited her out of the country, so she could be free. Free from what, doesn't matter she got her freedom. What did she do, she developed an entire new approach to psionic powers Quantomkinesis. <br /> <br /> Max/Mike (the oldest trick in the immortals book, making your self the son of your self, till he has to dip out to return as the grandson) <br /> So why does Max come back grumpy. Is it he is another version sort of, the books somewhat cover this, but this is not his first round the time line. It discussed in both aeon and abberant that major changes tend to make things worse, which implies that he tried to take a direct hand. This resulted in the worst of the first edition, ie the forced sterilization of the Novas, the fall out with the Project Utopia and Aeon Society. Even that was a result of Max knowing what the future holds, so even first edition wasn't his first trip through the timeline. So he is forced to work softly, unsure if it is even going to work this time. Max is exhausted, his grand daughter/ probably daughter has seen the changes in Max as he makes his jumps back and forth, cause at this time it probably is no longer an uncontrolled Quantum Leap scenario, now he just wants to save the world and his friends, he just doesn't know how to., and he has all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T20:16:16-07:00","id":1477609,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that the reason why TC Adventure defined Mercer's sexuality the way that it did was to avoid the problematic aspects of \u201cgay man loves straight man, but straight man doesn't reciprocate, so gay man goes crazy\u201d. Instead, it went with the notion that Mercer reciprocated Donegal feelings, but knew from his time hopping that it would be bad if he acted on his feelings. <br /> <br /> Given that the goal was to make things less problematic, the idea that Max had kids out of wedlock or in a loveless marriage strikes me as something else that would be avoided if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T20:41:57-07:00","id":1477613,"title":"","content":"They made Mercer's sexuality different to avoid being problematic? That doesn't make sense. I had the original Adventure! and though it is definitely apparent that Michael loved Maxwell I never got the feeling that it was what motivated him to go bad. In my game Max is going to be straight. I can't imagine a guy like him hiding who he is to have a kid just to match conventions of the time.<br /> <br /> I always thought of the original Trinity setting as a kind of philosophical battle between Max and Michael that Max ultimately wins when Michael takes his leave of Earth. Michael being in love with Max was sort of incidental to their friendship and philosophical differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T21:04:16-07:00","id":1477614,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that they made his sexuality different; in the original game, they never went into what Max's sexuality was at all. And as you say, they barely touched upon Michael's. In my humble opinion, they ended up making a mountain or of a molehill in TC:A!. My own approach to the master is to not bother with the subject; I much prefer focusing on, as you put it, the philosophical battle between the two; and I find the sexual elements to be an unwanted distraction from that. <br /> <br /> But that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-29-2022, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T02:32:51-07:00","id":1477621,"title":"","content":"As amusing as revisiting the &quot;Divis mal has arms !!1!&quot; thing in 2022 in a &quot;Max Mercer has legs!!1!&quot; version might be, until we get a canon detailed genealogy of the Mercer clan, I'm far more interested and confused by Max Mercer's personal timeline. <br /> <br /> We know that he started &quot;time skipping&quot; immediately after the Hammersmith incident while evacuating the wounded. Max Mercer tried to control the skips, and accidentally traveled to the future, initially &quot;as a helpless observer&quot;, and met MirrorMercer when he reached the Aeon era. His evil twin would have crushed him, but thanks to Hope and the Power of Hope/Friendship/ChasteLove, Max found his way back to Michael in his own time period and escaped. So far, Max has time traveled &quot;as a helpless observer&quot;. He's just seen the future, but hasn't interfered with it yet.<br /> <br /> Then Michael nurses him back to health and Max founds the Aeon Society hoping to course-correct the future he's seen. It doesn't seem to be working much and he retires from public life in the 1950s. At this point, Max now mastered his abilities enough that he is no longer &quot;a helpless observer&quot; when he travels in time, but he can't fix anything he foresees. When he tries to change the past to fix a future problem, he just creates a parallel universe where the problem is fixed, but the problem remains unchanged in the Original Timeline. I imagine that first half of the 20th century is when Max did the bulk of his time travel and created a gajillion alternate timelines.<br /> <br /> We know that Max and S.K. Bhurano compared notes about what they saw of the future, but I find myself wondering if as a clairsentient, she's bound by the same limitations Max is, or if she can course-correct the original timeline without the difficulties Max has. If so, it would be kind of a shame that she spent 200 years getting every Ph.D. ever instead of changing what Max couldn't.<br /> <br /> Smaller events do not create alternate timelines, but their effects are hard to predict. In theory, Max could still make the big changes to the original timeline by tipping the right domino at the right point in time, which I'm assuming is what he has been trying to do with limited success since the 1950s. I imagine that the only reason he remains involved with the Aeon Society is to keep it from veering too far off course and to maintain, through Aeon's far-reaching connections, access to whomever he needs to influence to make his targeted changes to the original timeline. His success remains a matter of debate : was he generally useless or would things have been much worse without him interfering discreetly here and there ? (Also, the targeted way that he's supposed to act to change the original timeline made me wonder if Lodestar/Lightkeepers would not be his scalpel answer to Aeon's hammer. Max Mercer as Pharos could be a fun twist.)<br /> <br /> tl;dr my Max Mercer Theory is that Max is Pharos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T08:21:42-07:00","id":1477629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477621#post1477621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As amusing as revisiting the &quot;Divis mal has arms !!1!&quot; thing in 2022 in a &quot;Max Mercer has legs!!1!&quot; version might be, until we get a canon detailed genealogy of the Mercer clan, I'm far more interested and confused by Max Mercer's personal timeline.<br /> <br /> We know that he started &quot;time skipping&quot; immediately after the Hammersmith incident while evacuating the wounded. Max Mercer tried to control the skips, and accidentally traveled to the future, initially &quot;as a helpless observer&quot;, and met MirrorMercer when he reached the Aeon era. His evil twin would have crushed him, but thanks to Hope and the Power of Hope/Friendship/ChasteLove, Max found his way back to Michael in his own time period and escaped. So far, Max has time traveled &quot;as a helpless observer&quot;. He's just seen the future, but hasn't interfered with it yet.<br /> <br /> Then Michael nurses him back to health and Max founds the Aeon Society hoping to course-correct the future he's seen. It doesn't seem to be working much and he retires from public life in the 1950s. At this point, Max now mastered his abilities enough that he is no longer &quot;a helpless observer&quot; when he travels in time, but he can't fix anything he foresees. When he tries to change the past to fix a future problem, he just creates a parallel universe where the problem is fixed, but the problem remains unchanged in the Original Timeline. I imagine that first half of the 20th century is when Max did the bulk of his time travel and created a gajillion alternate timelines.<br /> <br /> We know that Max and S.K. Bhurano compared notes about what they saw of the future, but I find myself wondering if as a clairsentient, she's bound by the same limitations Max is, or if she can course-correct the original timeline without the difficulties Max has. If so, it would be kind of a shame that she spent 200 years getting every Ph.D. ever instead of changing what Max couldn't.<br /> <br /> Smaller events do not create alternate timelines, but their effects are hard to predict. In theory, Max could still make the big changes to the original timeline by tipping the right domino at the right point in time, which I'm assuming is what he has been trying to do with limited success since the 1950s. I imagine that the only reason he remains involved with the Aeon Society is to keep it from veering too far off course and to maintain, through Aeon's far-reaching connections, access to whomever he needs to influence to make his targeted changes to the original timeline. His success remains a matter of debate : was he generally useless or would things have been much worse without him interfering discreetly here and there ? (Also, the targeted way that he's supposed to act to change the original timeline made me wonder if Lodestar/Lightkeepers would not be his scalpel answer to Aeon's hammer. Max Mercer as Pharos could be a fun twist.)<br /> <br /> tl;dr my Max Mercer Theory is that Max is Pharos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a thread discussing the possible origins of the lightkeepers, and my theory is pretty much the same: Max is Pharos. The only difference is that in my headcanon he created the lightkeepers to fight evil Mercer efforts to take over the timeline. Also, from my point of view, the aeon society exists to make the world a better place, while the lightkeepers exist to make sure it doesn't get worse. <br /> <br /> Now, regarding Max's ability to affect the timeline. My take on it is that Max's actions don't really make any significant changes, but when you put all the small changes together, the result is a world that overall is a little better: Wars still happen, but claim fewer lives and are shorter; economic recession puts millions in poverty, but the social net to help them is stronger; there's still corruption among politicians, but there's a stronger drive in society to not tolerate them and so on...<br /> <br /> His ability to time travel and change the timeline can't be too powerful, but it can't be useless either, otherwise what's the point of it?<br /> <br /> PD: (I completely forgot that Bhurano could also see the future. If that's the case, and she didn't do anything at all, then that's disappointing. Then again, perhaps after talking with Mercer about his failures she believes that it's best to focus on the present and not try to control the future?)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T09:05:08-07:00","id":1477632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477629#post1477629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PD: (I completely forgot that Bhurano could also see the future. If that's the case, and she didn't do anything at all, then that's disappointing. Then again, perhaps after talking with Mercer about his failures she believes that it's best to focus on the present and not try to control the future?)</div> </div> </div> </div>She and Mercer just couldn't agree on what to do about what they knew, and since Mercer refuses to share his inability to make sweeping changes to the original timeline, he looks somewhere between scared, lazy and negligent to Bhurano. That's why she chose to act through SFN and other groups instead of joining Aeon, but her knowledge of the future is way more limited. Max has actually been to the future whereas she's only gotten glimpses of it through Clairsentience <br /> <br /> She's in a weird in-between spot, and oddly enough, the one in closest proximity to humanity of the Big 3. Not knowing the reason why Mercer is so resistant to using his foreknowledge, Bhurano wants to actually push for political or social change, interestingly enough as a member of humanity herself, instead of gently nudging humanity forward as its wise and benevolent elite/superiors Aeon-Style, and she's keen to research Inspiration exhaustively, but doesn't feel the urgency to make humanity ascend <b>right now</b> that Donighal does with his <i>Inspired \u00fcber alles</i> outlook.<br /> <br /> Frankly, Max may have tried the honest approach with either or both of them and got shunted in a different timeline when he did, but it could also be that he's a poor communicator who knows how to lead but sucks at teamwork otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T12:42:42-07:00","id":1477640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1477603#post1477603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am politely reminding you you don\u2019t need to love to get married, you don\u2019t need to me married to have kids, and you don\u2019t need to accept your sexuality to be ok with other aspects of your life.<br /> <br /> In the time Max was born and the time we are discussing here there were lots of people living lives of lie to be accept by society, not only women were sexually repressed, men were forced to go to brothels with their fathers at young ages, and to those boys that didn\u2019t like women or didn\u2019t like the idea of prostitution, they were being raped by the prostitutes their fathers and friends were paying.<br /> <br /> Max can have kids and have lived for years married (between the 40s and the 80s) until his wife died of age or any disease in the gap between Adventure! and Aberrant, and yet being ace, gay, or any other sexual orientation, because by the time it was seen as wrong and sinful.<br /> <br /> I personally know more than one men in their 50s that after years married and having kids find out themselves as gay, just to leave their wives to embrace their sexuality and start dating man. And those are people that were born in the 60s and grew up after all the sexual revolution of the 60s and 70s. Imagine how many people denied their own self for their entire lives.<br /> <br /> In other words, summarizing, Max can be Ace and have kids, Max could be gay (actually love Michael romantically and sexually), not accept it (repressing his own sexuality) and have kids. Just don\u2019t say Max being *** would make it impossible for him to have biological kids (not to mention adoption).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some fundamental problems with your argument, which lead to other, bigger problems with your argument.<br /> <br /> Michael Mercer popped up out of nowhere after Max retired from public life sometime in the '50s, and lived until the late 2010s. If we assume sometime in the '50s equates to January 1, 1950, that means it has been a bit over 27 years since the Hammersmith event. How old is Michael? Is he older or younger than 27 years?<br /> <br /> The implication in the books is that Michael Mercer was an adult, but not pushing 30/in his 30s. If that is true, it indicates Michael Mercer was conceived AFTER Max was nursed back to health by Michael Donighal, fell in love with him, and rejected him because of their incompatible desires.<br /> <br /> The idea that he'd go from rejecting someone he genuinely loved to to knocking up some woman he didn't love and for whom he had no sexual attraction, and then named their kid after the man he loved but wouldn't screw is insulting to Michael Donighal and the moral character of Max Mercer.<br /> <br /> Do also note that, at the time of this supposed indiscretion, Max Mercer wouldn't have been a 'hormonal' youth, but instead would have been in his 30s or 40s, since he was old enough to get two undergraduate degrees and a masters degree, then care for his ailing father, then travel the world for years as a philanthropist, explorer, and guest lecturer. He was a wealthy man of the world, and in no position to be pressured to 'perform' due to social expectations.<br /> <br /> Even if that were the case, it wouldn't explain why no one knew of this child until he took over the AEon Society; after all, it doesn't help if you're pressured into having a kid for the sake of appearances, but never let anyone know you've had a kid. That kinda defeats the purpose of keeping up appearances.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you're claiming Michael Mercer was conceived when Max was in his early 20s? That would put him in his 40s when he popped up out of nowhere to take over, and that doesn't sound likely either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-29T13:07:13-07:00","id":1477641,"title":"","content":"I am not talking about Max having a son or not, I am talking about Max being able to have a son, even not being attracted to any one, that seams to be the main reason people don\u2019t think Michael is Max son. I agree with your complete calculations for Max and Michael ages and the timing.<br /> <br /> Michael as I see is an alternate Max or an alternate Max\u2019s son or Max\u2019s son he had in an alternate reality he (or Michael) can access somehow (pointing generally to the Mist artifacts from the Caper, Incorporated story from In Media Res), that end up in Max reality and helped him with Aeon after his way didn\u2019t work. That\u2019s MY head cannon, but so far it\u2019s not relevant in any situation in my life so far\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 03-29-2022, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T12:11:16-07:00","id":1477915,"title":"","content":"I don't see why Max has to be in romantic love with Michael, even ignoring the sexual aspect of it. Does it really matter if Max is straight or Ace if his orientation is incompatible with Michael's? Hell, as I recall even Micheal's sexual orientation is less important as he ages and increases in power, the physical desires associated with his orientation becoming more a biological relic of his past then something he actually experiences. In the Aberrant era isn't Divis Mal's relationship with Scripture sexless and perhaps even only marginally romantic?<br /> <br /> Max love Michael, but I don't see why he would have ever been <i>in love</i> with Michael.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T08:59:15-07:00","id":1478144,"title":"","content":"Of course another possibility is that Max is biromantic or homoromantic, but just not in love with Michael. Which also isn't incompatible with him being asexual or heterosexual, because humans are weird.<br /> <br /> By my understanding it kind of doesn't matter why Max doesn't want to be in a relationship with Michael, just that he isn't. On the other hand I'm only just getting into Trinity and haven't picked up Aberrant or Adventure! 1e yet, so I'm not sure if there's something deeper I'm not aware of. It's probably the kind of thing better to leave officially unclear so individual groups can decide for themselves why it didn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T12:29:12-07:00","id":1478162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1478144#post1478144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course another possibility is that Max is biromantic or homoromantic, but just not in love with Michael. Which also isn't incompatible with him being asexual or heterosexual, because humans are weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless things change from the Kickstarter manuscript to the printed book, Max did (to his own surprise) legitimately fall in love with Michael while convalescing after his uncontrolled Hammersmith Event time travel episode, but refused to enter into a relation due at least partially to his lack of physical attraction for anyone. This is one reason fans wonder where Max's supposed son, named Michael Maxwell, came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T14:06:58-07:00","id":1478165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1478162#post1478162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless things change from the Kickstarter manuscript to the printed book, Max did (to his own surprise) legitimately fall in love with Michael while convalescing after his uncontrolled Hammersmith Event time travel episode, but refused to enter into a relation due at least partially to his lack of physical attraction for anyone. This is one reason fans wonder where Max's supposed son, named Michael Maxwell, came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I haven't read the Adventure Kickstarter draft, but in my mind nothing's set in stone until release (although admittedly this sounds very unlikely to change, mainly because it just kind of doesn't matter).<br /> <br /> Heterosexual biromantic fits perfectly with him loving Michael but having a kid. Although admittedly other theories in this thread work perfectly as well, I like the 'a different version of Max contributed the materials' theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T02:26:24-07:00","id":1479227,"title":"","content":"Are there stats for Max and Micheal, especially in Adventure era?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T05:17:13-07:00","id":1482068,"title":"","content":"New informations about Max and Micheal in <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-jyhsu-13d875cf\" target=\"_blank\">Aberrant Secrets talk from OpCast</a><br /> <br /> One question - <b>What's the thing with Davis Mal and 'he has arms</b>'? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T07:35:30-07:00","id":1482072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1482068#post1482068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New informations about Max and Micheal in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-jyhsu-13d875cf&amp;quot;]Aberrant</a> Secrets talk from OpCast[/URL]<br /> <br /> One question - <b>What's the thing with Davis Mal and 'he has arms</b>'? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe his possession of arms, and the effect they've had on his life, is one of the biggest factors in how he acts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T10:40:14-07:00","id":1482080,"title":"","content":"Mal having arms was a sarcastic response to a post in a forum questioning the fact Mal was gay. Do you remember that post about the Katana being a master craft bastard sword with thousands of reactions when D&amp;D 3e was released? It\u2019s the same thing, but focused in Aberrant (but fighting homophobic comments, by the way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T18:20:18-07:00","id":1482113,"title":"","content":"It's strange, as I was envision by two-three years now that <i><b>'Davis Mal has arms'</b></i> means that he is so 'evolved' that he has like 3 pairs of arms, like Kali or Spider-man in crisis times. Reading previous and some spoilers, I supposed he become so <b>Aberrant </b>( Transcendent was 'higher being' state? ) he become inhuman - and <i><b>literally</b></i> get extra 2 pairs of arms.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.etsystatic.com/10036582/r/il/af4c5d/1343788931/il_570xN.1343788931_qsoj.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://qph.cf2.quoracdn.net/main-qimg-a0cd2d88350dd55c8373daeb03bcad4d.webp\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-27-2022, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T19:40:58-07:00","id":1482120,"title":"","content":"No. The idea was more like the guy says I can\u2019t believe Mal is gay, with a long text after, and the guy replied I can\u2019t believe Mal has Arms with a long text mirroring the first guy and being sarcastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T22:15:16-07:00","id":1485453,"title":"","content":"From first episode of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-from-the-depths-of-space-to-the-heart-of-london/\" target=\"_blank\">TC Aether 'serial'</a>...<br /> <br /> <i>Anne</i> Mercer? Mysterious J\u2014\u2014\u2014? What is going on here? \ud83d\ude32","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T19:50:03-07:00","id":1489292,"title":"","content":"In<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/vi-bows-and-arrows-against-the-lightning/\" target=\"_blank\"> last episode of Aether serial</a>, it's pointed that <b>Max Mercer was born deaf and learned sign language in childhood</b>. His parents, in Esoteric Order of Eons, debated to cure him by using Aether - but knew change would be temporal, like everything with Aether. ( So called 'unwinding'. ) However, we know that Max, in <b>Adventure</b> era ( 1923+ onward ) is not deaf. We also now that he jumped to circa 2120s ( Aeon era ) at least once, so maybe there he was cured of hearing problems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T01:01:18-07:00","id":1489300,"title":"","content":"If you are interested in Max Mercer life and stats - I invite you to this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1489201-tc-major-npcs-stats-across-eras?p=1489214#post1489214\">topic and post about his stats</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T03:55:40-07:00","id":1489309,"title":"","content":"I think he is not cured, but have an apparatus that let him perceive words (maybe hear, not properly explained). He probably was using a device to allow him to lister for most of his life at least until Hammersmith.<br /> <br /> Maybe he internalized this power using Edit Condition. Between you and me, Max was basically turned into a Magog by the Hammersmith accident, with no Magog gifts that change his appearance. Accelerate Tempo is basically his power as described in Adventure! (Not sure if D20 or 1e), probably with a personal method of Aether Gate to travel time. Eschew Mortality would be the only Magog gift he would have, but not sure what is the flaw of his immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T22:37:59-07:00","id":1491553,"title":"","content":"Quick sum up - <i><b>Maxwell Mercer</b></i> is superquick ( beside time travel powers ) and <i><b>Micheal Donighal</b></i>, a.k.a <i><b>Doctor Primoris</b></i>, is energy, heat, etc. resistant after Hammersmith Event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T23:11:48-07:00","id":1491557,"title":"","content":"No stats are given for them in TC:A!. In the original game, Max was given a \u201cChronal Awareness\u201d Knack which is described as a very versatile ability to manipulate time; in effect, he had the equivalent of five dots in the Time Sphere from Mage: the Ascension, or five dots in the Time Arcanum from Mage: the Awakening. Doctor Primoris, meanwhile, has \u201cmost of the level one and two Dynamic Knacks, and Dynamic versions of many Psychic Knacks\u201d. In TC:A! terms, he'd have a bunch of Dynamic Attribute Gifts; possibly some Dynamic Power Gifts (something that doesn't have a counterpart in the original game), and a number of unique Dynamic Gifts patterned after Psychic Gifts. Nothing as limited as \u201cresistant to energy, heat, etc.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T19:31:32-07:00","id":1491702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1491553#post1491553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Micheal Donighal</b></i>, a.k.a <i><b>Doctor Primoris</b></i>, is energy, heat, etc. resistant after Hammersmith Event?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what little we learn from his actions during and after the Hammersmith Event, he seems to have enhanced might, stamina, and intellect, as well as the ability to absorb fire and see through smoke. He may have enhanced resolve given his tunnel vision and resistance to being dissuaded from his path by Max Mercer and Dr. Bhurano. Anything beyond that amounts to giving him whatever powers you think he needs for your game.<br /> <br /> You don't have to give him all the powers like in 1st edition, since he's probably an outright Nova in a world of Stalwarts; he really is inherently more powerful than the others, so even a handful of Nova abilities outweigh a laundry list of Dynamic Gifts. He'll also eventually pioneer the Chrysalis process, which means he can swap powers to whatever he feels he needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T00:52:15-07:00","id":1492684,"title":"","content":"Okay, ST/SG question here - <b>HOW would you roleplay <i>Max Mercer</i> in adventure </b>( and <b>Adventure!</b> era \ud83d\ude0e )?<br /> <br /> I got it right that after Hammersmith and his time jumping 200 years in future he is kinda like 'positive Batman'? He acts a bit like rich playboy - but also not crossing the line of 'party boy', just <i>'rich, owning it, crazy adventurer - but also philanthropist'</i>. He saw future, he <b><u>knows</u></b> world can ( and should ) be better in next decades. But also he likes to act and is a bit intense. ( <i>Somehow</i> like Batman, I think? Or maybe <b>Green Arrow's</b> <i>Oliver Queen</i> as Social Justice Warrior of that era? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2022, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T05:31:31-07:00","id":1492692,"title":"","content":"I think of Max as closer to Oliver Queen than Bruce Wayne in personality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T05:34:45-07:00","id":1492693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492684#post1492684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, ST/SG question here - <b>HOW would you roleplay <i>Max Mercer</i> in adventure </b>( and <b>Adventure!</b> era \ud83d\ude0e )?<br /> <br /> I got it right that after Hammersmith and his time jumping 200 years in future he is kinda like 'positive Batman'? He acts a bit like rich playboy - but also not crossing the line of 'party boy', just <i>'rich, owning it, crazy adventurer - but also philanthropist'</i>. He saw future, he <b><u>knows</u></b> world can ( and should ) be better in next decades. But also he likes to act and is a bit intense. ( <i>Somehow</i> like Batman, I think? Or maybe <b>Green Arrow's</b> <i>Oliver Queen</i> as Social Justice Warrior of that era? )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For me, Max Mercer is the eternal optimist, a true man of hope. He believes in a better tomorrow because he has literally been there, but he also understands that if you want a better future, you have to make it real by working hard in the present. When I role-play him, I always go with the gentleman adventurer angle: Calm, charming, impeccable manners, a compassionate look that tells you that everything will be alright and a contagious enthusiasm that makes you want to be the best version of yourself. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T11:30:19-07:00","id":1492705,"title":"","content":"I like the idea Divis Mal started out as basically a bitter, cynical Randall Portman. I wonder when it was Mal learnt to turn the \u2018fire valve\u2019, so to speak, in the other direction, ie, when he develop Quantum Attack and Quantum Anima?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T13:26:57-07:00","id":1492710,"title":"","content":"The thing about Max Mercer is that he <b>can't</b> give orders. Any direct action he takes to alter history will produce a new timeline instead of changing the old one, so he's forced to poke around the edges of major events through intermediaries and hope for the best. I figure he uses something similar to Socratic dialogue to get his agents to answer their own questions, only introducing new facts in response to their actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T16:31:44-07:00","id":1492721,"title":"","content":"Kind of like Greek myth\u2019s Cassandra, huh? She knew the future, but by spurning Apollo she was cursed to never be believed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T23:34:18-07:00","id":1492786,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is simple Aspiration list for Max Mercer in 1923. I based him on your points, but mainly <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2964_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2964\" data-vbnamecard=\"2964\">Firanai</a> take on character. What do you think about this goals for him?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Max Aspirations</b></span><br /> <b>Short</b> \u2013 Find <i>\u2018Future Sight\u2019 </i>relic ( to understand future better )<br /> <b>Short</b> \u2013 INSPIRE someone to be better in life/particular event<br /> <b>Long </b>\u2013 Build Better Future ( Create 1923 Aeon Society for starters )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T09:37:01-07:00","id":1492808,"title":"","content":"\u2018Future Sight\u2019 relic? What exactly do you mean by that? An piece of Inspired science that can help Mercer look into the future? Or something else, entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T20:02:12-07:00","id":1492851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492808#post1492808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2018Future Sight\u2019 relic? What exactly do you mean by that? An piece of Inspired science that can help Mercer look into the future? Or something else, entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it's not directly tied to Mercer himself - only to the story I run with him - I invite all interested to the <b>Aeon Society creation story topic</b>, for more info on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story?p=1492850#post1492850\"><b>Future Sight relic</b></a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T20:06:10-07:00","id":1492853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492684#post1492684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, ST/SG question here - <b>HOW would you roleplay <i>Max Mercer</i> in adventure </b>( and <b>Adventure!</b> era \ud83d\ude0e )?</div> </div> </div> </div>Got another nice answer on Max on unofficial Trinity Discord:<br /> <i>I sorta imagine Max as seeming lika almost a paragon of patience. Not only has he seen the future, he's seen a lot of futures, and recognises that small acts can have powerful effects on the future. So, he tends towards compassion, at least as he understands it, believing that small, compassionate acts could well have the same impact as the Big Projects like the \u00c6on Society in making the world better Indeed, that's kinda the most annoying thing about him - he has an unshakeable belief that, no matter the dire catastrophe, or the clear destruction he sees, he knows humanity will come out alright, maybe even better than they started. He still does his best to save life's and mitigate damage, but he never feels like he really takes the gravity of existentialn threats into account?</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T06:53:37-07:00","id":1492880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492853#post1492853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got another nice answer on Max on unofficial Trinity Discord:<br /> <i>I sorta imagine Max as seeming as almost a paragon of patience. Not only has he seen the future, he's seen a lot of futures, and recognizes that small acts can have powerful effects on the future. So, he tends towards compassion, at least as he understands it, believing that small, compassionate acts could well have the same impact as the Big Projects like the \u00c6on Society in making the world better Indeed, that's kinda the most annoying thing about him - he has an unshakable belief that, no matter the dire catastrophe, or the clear destruction he sees, he knows humanity will come out alright, maybe even better than they started. He still does his best to save life's and mitigate damage, but he never feels like he really takes the gravity of existential threats into account?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That make sense. Max more than anyone else knows just how much the circumstances of our life shape who we become, he has literally seen it in different timelines. That's why he gives everyone a chance and, for the most part, approaches people without judgement. The most despicable villain could have become an amazing person had he only grown up in a different place. This doesn't mean he automatically forgives everyone, it means that for him everyone can become a better version of themselves and deserve a chance to prove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T10:55:32-07:00","id":1492897,"title":"","content":"I dunno, it feels to me at least that Mercer is willing to allow millions to suffer, if it means billions prosper, later on. He could have talked Donighal out of instrumenting N-Day, and stopped the horrors of the Aberrant Wars, but he saw that, while humanity would go through a period of absolute hell, there was light at the end of the tunnel.<br /> <br /> In fact, there seem to have been a lot of things Mercer could have done, but didn\u2019t. His \u2018compassion\u2019, at least to me, is tainted by a very real sense of brutal pragmatism. The needs of the many FAR outweigh the needs of the few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T11:56:32-07:00","id":1492907,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492897#post1492897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, it feels to me at least that Mercer is willing to allow millions to suffer, if it means billions prosper, later on. He could have talked Donighal out of instrumenting N-Day, and stopped the horrors of the Aberrant Wars, but he saw that, while humanity would go through a period of absolute hell, there was light at the end of the tunnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to assume that Michael Donighal - an adult man of superhuman intellect and (possibly) superhuman stubbornness - has no agency of his own, and would have obviously done whatever Max Mercer told him to do if Max had bothered to give the order. This is the opposite of the truth. According to the Adventure! manuscript, Max tried many, many times to deter Donighal from his course, then tried getting Sara Bhurano to dissuade him as well.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The start of the \u04d4on Society was a golden time, but soon Doctor Primoris\u2019s and Max\u2019s philosophies began to diverge. As much as Max tried to guide him, Doctor Primoris became more single-minded in his pursuit. He watched as the man he loved withdrew deeper into himself, and eventually broke away from him.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sara reached out to Doctor Primoris, and all the way through the 1940s, she kept up a professional relationship with him, sharing her research and notes about the Inspired and telluric energy. She tried to guide him towards the path she wanted him on, but knew she had minimal influence over him. She urged Max Mercer to help her, and his refusal confused and bothered her. She had no idea that Max had already tried several times, but doing so just created alternate timelines. Not knowing this degraded her trust in him and the \u00c6on Society, leaving her to work with other organizations instead.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Not only did he try to change things, he tried so hard he permanently alienated one of his close allies. You're blaming Reed Richards for Doctor Doom's crimes.<br /> <br /> As for him choosing not to stop the Aberrant War:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Afraid of the Aberrant War and everything that it causes in the future, Max tried several times to prevent it from happening. Doing so was rarely successful, as the event is tied to too many different factors. The one time he actually succeeded, he believed he had saved his future. But when he returned to his own time, he realized that he was in a completely alternate timeline, a different dimension that was extremely close to his own in which the Aberrant War never happens. He had not prevented the war, but instead slipped sideways into a branching timeline. This proved to be the case for every major incident Max tried to correct or manipulate. At one point, he had created so many alternate timelines that he spent a week trying to untangle it and find his way home.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> He did try. He tried over and over again. He failed every time, because any attempt to prevent the war spawns a new timeline; the war always happens and there is nothing he can do to stop it. All he managed was to say the words that convinced Divis Mal to leave the world rather than fight it out and doom everyone.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1441517-trinity-continuum-max-mercer-theory?p=1492897#post1492897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, there seem to have been a lot of things Mercer could have done, but didn\u2019t. His \u2018compassion\u2019, at least to me, is tainted by a very real sense of brutal pragmatism. The needs of the many FAR outweigh the needs of the few.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> What brutal pragmatism? Max Mercer is a man who cannot directly change the future, because he's already been there. Any attempt to directly interfere with future events splits off a new timeline. It was his frustration over his inability to change things no matter how hard he tried that lead him to retire from public involvement with Aeon in the 1950s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T15:52:14-07:00","id":1492931,"title":"","content":"Ah. I did not have access to the TC Adventure! material. I happily withdraw my assertion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T00:28:08-07:00","id":1492961,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm surprised that Max hasn't gone outright insane. Just imagine seeing the same tragic events playing over and over again with no power to make any significant changes. At some point, you just give up or go nuts. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T08:53:44-07:00","id":1492978,"title":"","content":"Maybe he <i>did</i> give up....for awhile, at least. He vanished for awhile, and left his granddaughter in charge. Maybe Max took a sabbatical? Y\u2019know, took some \u201cMe\u201d-time, recharged his batteries, before returning to the struggle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T14:17:40-07:00","id":1493283,"title":"","content":"My players are THE WORST - ( or I am on NPC roleplay ) - First they talk with Mercer in 1923 - they get from him that he saw 100 years into the future... \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if Mercer would be more closed up on the matter to